    "searchCoverage": "AppleDB is a community-maintained MIT static JSON API. Pinned source is no_auth. get_device and get_os_build are simple GETs. search_devices downloads /device/main.json and filters in-process. search_os_builds downloads an ICS calendar and parses it. Native auth is api_key or oauth2; no_auth has no secret. No authenticated healthcheck exists. littlebyteorg/emiyl has no evidenced registered-company country in this review. Dated incident search on 2026-09-13 found no qualifying unresolved AppleDB compromise.",
    "incidents": [],
    "remainingGates": [
      "credentials: pinned authTypes is no_auth. Native setup is api_key or oauth2; inventing a dummy secret would be untruthful.",
      "healthcheck: AppleDB takes no credentials. Pinned 401/403 are treated as WAF/bot blocks, not reconnect prompts. There is no cheap authenticated account GET.",
      "operationQuality: search_devices is client-side fanout of /device/main.json; search_os_builds is ICS parse (unsupported). Operator geography/company country was not evidenced beyond the GitHub org and emiyl.com personal site.",
      "live authentication unverified"
    ],
    "waiverAuthority": "User waiver dated 2026-09-13 permits historical non-China incident coverage."
